.TH SETUP 1 "2026-08-31" "SPS 1.0" "SPS Commands"
.SH NAME
setup \- dialog-based SPS Linux installer (Splux)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
setup [options]
setup --list-profiles
setup --list-sets
setup --plan [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup
installs
.B SPS Linux
(informally Splux) into a target root. It is the distro installer, not a
generic Linux From Scratch helper. SPS the package system can be used on
other trees without running this program; partitioning, users, and boot
layout on those trees are yours to decide.
.PP
Interactive use is a sequence of
.BR dialog (1)
screens in the same spirit as the Slackware and FreeBSD installers: profile,
optional package sets, extra packages, locale, hostname, timezone, keymap,
first user, login shell, then a visible package build.
.PP
Every screen has a command-line equivalent. Scripts and tests should pass
.B --non-interactive
or
.B --plan .
.B --plan
does not start
.BR dialog (1).
.PP
The installer does not run
.B grub-install
unless
.B --install-bootloader
is given with
.B --disk .
Guided partitioning waits until the last confirmation.
.B --init systemd
or
.B --init openrc
selects PID 1;
.B sget
will not install both.
Live images prefer systemd. If the build host has no systemd binaries,
busybox init runs instead and respawns gettys on tty1 and ttyS0.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B minimal
.B base-system
and
.BR dialog (1).
.TP
.B server
Minimal plus OpenSSH, GnuPG, rsync, and sudo.
.TP
.B plasma-desktop
KDE Plasma session without the full application suite.
.TP
.B plasma-full
Plasma plus
.BR kde-apps ,
Firefox, and Flatpak.
.SH SETS
Optional sets are listed by
.B --list-sets
and stored as text files under
.I $SPS_LIBDIR/setup/sets .
They include quality-of-life CLI tools, development tools, language
toolchains, KDE applications, NVIDIA drivers, Flatpak, power management,
multimedia, extra network tools, extra editors, container helpers, printing,
browsers, extra shells, extra fonts, office tools, and OpenSSH.
.PP
.B plasma-desktop
and
.B plasma-full
turn the power and qol-cli sets on by default.
.B --enable
adds sets.
.B --disable
removes them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target " dir"
Installation root. Must be an absolute path. Becomes
.B SPS_ROOT
for
.BR src (1)
and
.BR sget (1).
.TP
.BI --profile " name"
One of the profiles above.
.TP
.BI --enable " set[,set...]"
.TP
.BI --disable " set[,set...]"
.TP
.BI --hostname " name"
.TP
.BI --timezone " zone"
.TP
.BI --keymap " map"
.TP
.BI --locale " name"
.B LANG
written to
.I /etc/locale.conf .
Default
.BR C.UTF-8 .
.TP
.BI --shell " path"
Login shell for the first user. Default
.IR /bin/sh .
Choosing zsh or fish also enables the
.B shells-extra
set.
.TP
.BI --extra " pkg[,pkg...]"
Individual packages in addition to the profile and sets.
.TP
.B --ssh yes|no
Enable the OpenSSH set.
.TP
.B --printing yes|no
Enable CUPS and related printing packages.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
First unprivileged account (uid 1000). The password is left locked; see
.I /root/sps-user.txt .
.TP
.B --flatpak yes|no
Install the Flatpak set and attempt to add Flathub after packages land.
.TP
.B --init systemd|openrc
PID 1 on the installed system. Scripts default to none so a fixture
install does not pull systemd. The interactive screen defaults to
systemd.
.TP
.B --nvidia yes|no
Install NVIDIA open kernel modules and utilities. A matching kernel is
required; this installer does not build one.
.TP
.B --bootloader none|grub
Write notes only.
.TP
.B --install-bootloader
Refuses to guess a disk. See the notes file.
.TP
.B --no-update
Skip
.B src update
before
.B sget install .
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Never start
.BR dialog (1).
.TP
.B --plan
Print the resolved configuration and package list, then exit.
.TP
.BI --write-answers " file"
.TP
.BI --read-answers " file"
Options override values from the file.
.TP
.B --list-profiles
.TP
.B --list-sets
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $SPS_LIBDIR/setup
Profiles, sets, keymaps, and timezones.
.TP
.I $SPS_SETUP_DIR
Optional override of that directory, used by tests.
.TP
.I /etc/sps/setup-answers
Copy of the resolved answers in the target root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 for usage errors, 3 when a profile or set is unknown,
8 for permission problems, 9 when
.B src update
fails, and 10 when package installation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dialog (1),
.BR sget (1),
.BR src (1),
.BR pkin (1)
